# What must never reach the frontend build context.
#
# This file governs the `frontend/` context only - the build is run as
# `docker build ./frontend`, so Docker reads THIS .dockerignore and not the
# repository-root one. The root file stays untouched and keeps excluding
# `frontend/` from the API build; the two contexts are independent by design.
#
# NOTE on pattern depth: a pattern without "**" only matches at the ROOT of
# the context. The same lesson the API image learned with stale __pycache__
# applies here, so anything that could exist at more than one depth is written
# with `**/`.

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The entry that matters most. frontend/.env holds the real CRM_API_KEY. An
# image can be pushed to a registry, pulled, and inspected layer by layer: a
# .env baked into one is a credential published, and no later deletion removes
# it from the layer that added it.
#
# The Dockerfile copies named files rather than `COPY . .`, so this is defence
# in depth - but it is the defence that must never be the one that was
# missing.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.json

# --- Node ------------------------------------------------------------------
# ~2,300 files. `npm ci` reinstalls them inside the builder from the lockfile,
# so sending the host copy would be both wasteful and wrong: a tree built on
# Windows can carry platform-specific binaries that do not run on linux.
**/node_modules/
**/.npm/
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
# dist/ is PRODUCED by the builder stage, never imported into it. Sending a
# local copy risks the image serving whatever happened to be on the developer
# machine - a bundle built against different sources, possibly months old -
# instead of the one built from the committed code a moment earlier.
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local

# --- Version control -------------------------------------------------------
# Not just size: history can hold values that were removed from the working
# tree but still exist in an old commit.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Docker's own files ----------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in the build reads them; excluding them keeps a Dockerfile edit from
# invalidating the context checksum.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# --- Documentation ---------------------------------------------------------
# Useful in the repository, dead weight in a running container.
**/*.md

# --- Editors and OS --------------------------------------------------------
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Logs and scratch ------------------------------------------------------
**/*.log
logs/
tmp/
